WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:04.879
I was only 17
when I first applied to do ROTC.

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.381
I didn't come
from a military family,

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.967
so it wasn't really something
we expected.

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.720
But after that, ended up
sticking with it.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.638
Now I'm here.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.350
My name is Brandon Colas.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.935
I'm an Army lieutenant colonel.

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:20.729
I've been in the service
for 17 years now

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:22.439
and I’m a foreign area officer.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.733
I’m here at Yale. It's my first
year in the

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.359
political science PhD program.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:29.070
Yale has a long history
of veterans service

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.406
being part of this community
of scholars,

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.325
at least for me, there's
been something satisfying in

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:37.620
whether you served a full career
or just for a few years,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.414
you joined something
that was a lot

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:41.583
bigger than yourself
and made a commitment.

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:42.834
And there's something

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.670
honorable and special in that,
and it gives me great

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.339
pride to be a
part of that along with you.

